WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.239
What happens when we split one whole into
smaller equal

2
00:00:03.309 --> 00:00:07.477
parts? The same base ten pattern continues
beyond the decimal

3
00:00:07.546 --> 00:00:11.970
point. After ones come tenths, hundredths
and thousandths.

4
00:00:12.504 --> 00:00:14.954
Each place is one tenth of the value of
the

5
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.626
place immediately to its left.

6
00:00:17.264 --> 00:00:19.261
Read four point seven two six.

7
00:00:19.876 --> 00:00:21.490
The four is four ones.

8
00:00:22.001 --> 00:00:25.275
The seven is seven tenths, written zero
point seven.

9
00:00:25.913 --> 00:00:29.024
The two is two hundredths, written zero
point zero two.

10
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:32.484
The six is six thousandths, written zero
point zero zero

11
00:00:32.554 --> 00:00:34.446
six. Put the parts together.

12
00:00:34.922 --> 00:00:38.255
Four point seven two six equals four, plus
zero point

13
00:00:38.313 --> 00:00:42.133
seven, plus zero point zero two, plus zero
point zero

14
00:00:42.202 --> 00:00:46.370
zero six. The digits describe different
sized parts, so their

15
00:00:46.428 --> 00:00:48.866
positions matter just as much as they do
in whole

16
00:00:48.901 --> 00:00:51.420
numbers. A tenth is ten hundredths.

17
00:00:51.905 --> 00:00:53.937
A hundredth is ten thousandths.

18
00:00:54.262 --> 00:00:58.163
Now compare zero point five with zero
point zero five.

19
00:00:58.523 --> 00:01:02.911
Five tenths is ten times five hundredths,
so zero point

20
00:01:02.981 --> 00:01:05.930
five is greater. The same digit does not
mean the

21
00:01:05.977 --> 00:01:09.355
same value. Think of a measuring scale
marked in equal

22
00:01:09.425 --> 00:01:13.918
small steps. Thousandths let us describe
positions more precisely than

23
00:01:14.011 --> 00:01:18.529
hundredths. This is about understanding
place value, not just counting

24
00:01:18.599 --> 00:01:20.340
how many digits come after the point.

25
00:01:20.921 --> 00:01:23.638
Keep the whole and the size of each part
clear.

26
00:01:24.079 --> 00:01:27.027
Try the page example: three point four
five eight.

27
00:01:27.434 --> 00:01:30.209
The five is in the hundredths place, so
its value

28
00:01:30.232 --> 00:01:32.066
is zero point zero five.

29
00:01:32.507 --> 00:01:36.443
Remember: ones, tenths, hundredths,
thousandths.

30
00:01:36.887 --> 00:01:40.567
Every step right divides the place value
by ten; every

31
00:01:40.625 --> 00:01:42.785
step left makes it ten times as much.

